WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:04.248
This is the technical deep dive
for a companion guide in the

3
00:00:04.248 --> 00:00:08.587
Federal Modernization Workbook:
Ansible for Configuration Automation.

4
00:00:08.587 --> 00:00:10.974
It's for the engineers
who decide which tool

5
00:00:10.974 --> 00:00:13.625
may change which setting,
and prove it afterward.

6
00:00:13.625 --> 00:00:16.187
The guide's idea fits in one line.

7
00:00:16.187 --> 00:00:20.521
Ansible can reach almost anything
with an S S H port or an A P I,

8
00:00:20.521 --> 00:00:25.738
so a program has to decide, setting by
setting, where it's allowed to write.

9
00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:28.963
Anything the guide couldn't
confirm stays labeled that way.

10
00:00:28.963 --> 00:00:30.840
Let's start with why this matters.
